# Line endings
# ============
#
# Everything is stored with LF in the repository AND checked out with LF, on
# every platform. That is what silences the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" wall
# of warnings, and it is the right call for this repository specifically:
#
#   - The course is driven from Git Bash and Herd's CLI, both of which want LF.
#   - `git-setup.sh` and any future shell script BREAK with CRLF endings. Bash
#     reads the trailing \r as part of the command and reports errors like
#     `$'\r': command not found`, which is a genuinely confusing failure for
#     somebody who has just cloned the repo.
#   - PHP itself is indifferent to line endings, so nothing is lost.
#
# The one thing to know: Windows Notepad renders LF-only files as a single long
# line. Any real editor — VS Code, PhpStorm, Sublime, vim — is fine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF. Stated separately so that the rule survives anyone
# relaxing the line above.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.sqlite  binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db      binary
